messages.body_plain:
For efficiency, you don't ever want to do the same calculation
twice.  You have lots of repeated (y - mu) and sqrt(mu).

The problem is that for a Poisson, the rate parameter mu must
be positive.  The usual solution is to think of mu instead as the
log of the mean, apply exp() to it and use that, as in:

  y ~ poisson(exp(mu));

which would be coded in Stan more robustly as:

 y ~ poisson_log(mu);

at which point I'd suggest renaming mu to log_mu.

- Bob

